AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:OBIB_0002112 "http://ncicb.nci.nih.gov/xml/owl/EVS/Thesaurus.owl#C71104")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBIB_0002112 "A research study that prospectively assigns human participants or groups of humans to one or more health-related interventions to evaluate the effects on health outcomes.")
SubClassOf(obo:OBIB_0002112 obo:OBIB_0002042)
Declaration(Class(obo:OBIB_0002113))
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:OBIB_0002113 "forth")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBIB_0002113 "A research study is considered broadly to be any scientific activity aimed at answering a research question. Studies can be simple or complex, depending on the scope of the question being explored and the extent of resources deployed in doing so. They may include a full research investigation, a set of experiments, or a single experiment or assay. Regardless, that act of summarizing any results as a finding statement is considered part of the study. A research study is considered broadly to be any scientific activity aimed at answering a research question. Studies can be simple or complex, depending on the scope of the question being explored and the extent of resources deployed in doing so. They may include a full research investigation, a set of related experiments, or a single experiment or assay. Regardless, that act of summarizing any results as a finding statement is considered part of the study. 'Study' here is broadly considered to include any defined activity performed to address a scientific question or generate a scientific hypothesis. It covers scientific inquiry at different scales of complexity, from a single assay, experiment or observation, to a complex research investigation addressing a broader scientific question. Studies can be based on a broad range of methods, including in silico algorithms, in vitro or in vivo experimentation on model systems, clinical studies on human subjects, or curation and analysis of existing knowledge, e.g. from publications, datasets, or knowledegbases, to derive novel insight. A planned process that executes some study design or protocol to generate scientific data that is interpreted to test or generate a hypothesis.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:OBIB_0002113 "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/SEPIO_0000125")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBIB_0002113 "research study"@en)
SubClassOf(obo:OBIB_0002113 obo:OBIB_0002042)
Declaration(Class(obo:OBIB_0002114))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBIB_0002114 "public health or population based study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBIB_0002114 "A sample collection setting in which biological specimens are collected as part of a public health initiative or population-based study for surveillance, epidemiological research, or health assessment.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:OBIB_0002114 "forth")
SubClassOf(obo:OBIB_0002114 obo:OBIB_0002042)
