Declaration(Class(obo:OBI_0000103))
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000232 obo:OBI_0000103 "CDISC definition: A person responsible for the conduct of the clinical trial at a trial site. If a trial is conducted by a team of individuals at a trial site, the investigator is the responsible leader of the team and may be called the principal investigator. 2. The individual principal investigator. 2. The individual under whose immediate direction the test article is administered or dispensed to, or used involving, a subject, or, in the event of an investigation conducted by a team of individuals, is See also sponsor-investigator.; Leiter der klinischen Prufung.Under the German Drug Law, the physician who is head of the clinical investigation (CDISC): coordinating investigator (CDISC) (also study coordinator, MUSC); sponsor-investigator. An individual who both initiates and conducts, alone or with others, a clinical trial, and under whose immediate direction the investigational product is administered to, dispensed to, or used by a subject.NOTE: The term does not include any person other than an individual, hence not a corporation, agency (CDISC)"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBI_0000103 "a responsible party role played by a person responsible for the overall conduct of a study"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:OBI_0000103 obo:IAO_0000123)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000111 obo:OBI_0000103 "principal investigator role")
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBI_0000103 "principal investigator role"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:OBI_0000103 "principal investigator")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:OBI_0000103 "Person: Jennifer Fostel"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:OBI_0000103 obo:obi.owl)
SubClassOf(obo:OBI_0000103 obo:OBI_0000102)
Declaration(Class(obo:OBI_0000112))
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:OBI_0000112 "Note: definition is in specimen creation objective which is defined as an objective to obtain and store a material entity for potential use as an input during an investigation.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000111 obo:OBI_0000112 "specimen role")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000119 obo:OBI_0000112 "OBI")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:OBI_0000112 "22Jun09.  The definition includes whole organisms, and can include a human.  The link between specimen role and study subject role has been removed.  A specimen taken as part of a case study is not considered to be a population representative, while a specimen taken as representing a population, e.g. person taken from a cohort, blood specimen taken from an animal) would be considered a population representative and would also bear material sample role.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000112 obo:OBI_0000112 "liver section; a portion of a culture of cells; a nemotode or other animal once no longer a subject (generally killed); portion of blood from a patient.")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:OBI_0000112 obo:obi.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:OBI_0000112 <https://github.com/obi-ontology/obi/issues/1013>)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:OBI_0000112 "a role borne by a material entity that is gained during a specimen collection process and that can be realized by use of the specimen in an investigation"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:OBI_0000112 "specimen role"@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:OBI_0000112 "parasite example
- when parasite in people we study people, people are subjects and parasites are specimen
- when parasite extracted, they become subject in the following study
specimen can later be subject."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000114 obo:OBI_0000112 obo:IAO_0000122)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:OBI_0000112 "blood taken from animal: animal continues in study, whereas blood has role specimen.
something taken from study subject, leaves the study and becomes the specimen."@en)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000117 obo:OBI_0000112 "GROUP:  Role Branch")
