AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000165 "The proximal portion of the digestive tract, containing the oral cavity and bounded by the oral opening. In vertebrates, this extends to the pharynx and includes gums, lips, tongue and parts of the palate. Typically also includes the teeth, except where these occur elsewhere (e.g. pharyngeal jaws) or protrude from the mouth (tusks).")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000118 obo:UBERON_0000165 "regio oralis")
SubClassOf(obo:UBERON_0000165 obo:UBERON_0000465)
Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0000173))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:UBERON_0000173 "amniotic fluid")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:UBERON_0000173 obo:uberon.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000173 "Amniotic fluid is a bodily fluid consisting of watery liquid surrounding and cushioning a growing fetus within the amnion. It allows the fetus to move freely without the walls of the uterus being too tight against its body. Buoyancy is also provided. The composition of the fluid changes over the course of gestation. Initially, amniotic fluid is similar to maternal plasma, mainly water with electrolytes. As the fetus develops, proteins, carbohydrates, lipids, phospholipids originating from the lungs, fetal cells, and urea are deposited in the fluid.")
SubClassOf(obo:UBERON_0000173 obo:UBERON_0000463)
