Declaration(Class(obo:UBERON_0000341))
AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:UBERON_0000341 "throat")
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000412 obo:UBERON_0000341 obo:uberon.owl)
AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:UBERON_0000341 "In anatomy, the throat is the anterior part of the neck, in front of the vertebral column. It consists of the pharynx and larynx. An important feature of the throat is the epiglottis, a flap which separates the esophagus from the trachea and prevents inhalation of food or drink. The throat contains various blood vessels, various pharyngeal muscles, the trachea (windpipe) and the esophagus. The hyoid bone and the clavicle are the only bones located in the throat of mammals. It is sometimes considered a synonym for fauces. [WP,unvetted].")
SubClassOf(obo:UBERON_0000341 obo:UBERON_0000465)
